\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
\ src/pow.fam — memory-hard proof-of-work hash (Poseidon2-BabyBear, 32 rounds).
\ Verifier side: given a block header and the pre-expanded bible slot-hash table,
\ recompute the PoW hash. Mirrors tmp/tabernacle.bak2/src/pow.rs but ROUNDS=32
\ (1024->32 so the PoW fits the zk-STARK; trades some memory-hardness) and uses
\ Poseidon2 (the reference already moved the round mix off XOR to compress2 for
\ in-circuit tractability). Built on p2hash (poseidon2.fam) + wcompr2 (wotsp.fam);
\ compile AFTER both. NO alloc-per-call: caller passes the slot table + scratch.
\   powhash ( hdr n table mask out scr -- )
\     out(8w) = state; state = p2hash(hdr,n); 32x: idx = state[0]&mask;
\     state = compress2(state, table + idx*0x20). scr>=0xA0.
\ table = SLOT_COUNT * 8 words (pre-expanded, shipped — NOT expanded at runtime:
\ expansion is ~16.7M Poseidon2 hashes, impractical in QEMU). Production mask =
\ 0x7FFFF (524288 slots); ROUNDS stays 32. Python ref: tmp/pos2/powref.py.
\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

: powhash ( hdr n table mask out scr -- )
  5 lit pick 5 lit pick 3 lit pick 3 lit pick p2hash
  20 lit 0 lit do
    1 lit pick  2 lit pick @ 4 lit pick and  5 lit pick swap 5 lit lshift +  1 lit pick 3 lit pick wcompr2
  loop
  2drop 2drop 2drop ;

